00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:53.270
Aren't you hungry too, Dandy?

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:58.820
At times like this, this guy's probably looking for a cute server.

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:01.450
<i>Even</i> at times like this, you mean.

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:03.620
Besides, it's not the face I care about—

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:04.740
It's the <i>ass</i>!

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:05.740
Is that so?

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:07.410
Don't rush!

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:10.160
Slow and steady wins the race, baby.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:15.590
Slow and Steady Wins the Race, Baby

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:15.590
Slow and Steady Wins the Race, Baby

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:17.340
Ta-da!

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:24.550
This is a teleportation light called Mr. Teleporter.

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:30.060
It's a wonderful advice that can teleport anything its light is beamed on.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:31.440
Isn't it amazing?

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.940
I thought you were going to buy <i>food</i>!

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:36.730
Oh, shut up.

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:40.990
If we have this, we could do this and that, 
and then that'll happen,

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:43.780
and we'll be able to eat as much as we want.

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:45.570
That's too roundabout!

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:49.250
Just because the girl at the store was a <i>little</i> "boing" with a <i>little</i> waist and curvy hips...

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:50.790
It wasn't just a little"!

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:53.080
She was pretty close to Dandy's ideal.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:57.090
Don't you know the story of the straw millionaire?

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:59.170
I don't really know it either.

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:00.090
You don't?

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:03.680
The point is, good things come to those who wait.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:06.390
Those people in the past had some good sayings.

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:08.890
Are you taking this seriously?!

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:27.200
What is this place?

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:32.100
Hey!

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:42.400
Welcome!!
 I am the first astronaut 
to come to
 Planet Pushy Boyfriend.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.280
My name is 
Baked or Boiled or Carpaccio!!

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:49.320
Nice to meet you!!

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:55.410
You are the first alien 
my people have ever encountered.

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:58.330
I am very moved 
and excited.

00:05:58.330 --> 00:05:59.830
I am so extremely honored!!

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:01.840
I have no idea what he's saying.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.880
Where are you from?

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:10.220
Do you live here?

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:16.930
Do you move 
with just your head?

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:23.860
It doesn't look like 
you have any arms or legs.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:27.860
I can't do gestures, either.

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:38.910
Is he dancing?

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:43.790
Aren't those calisthenics?

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:46.840
No, I think those are gestures.

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:48.760
I wonder what he's trying to say.

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:51.550
Maybe "I'm the best!" or something?

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:53.800
Or "I want to eat crayfish!"?

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:17.330
That is my planet.

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:28.800
It was pulled in by the gravity of this planet and became it's satellite several hundred years ago.

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:38.430
Aren't we in trouble?

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:48.610
It's a halibut!! Run!!

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:50.240
Are we okay?

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:53.780
It looks like we're slipping over the ground.

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:55.780
We're traveling.

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:59.160
We're riding on an invisible giant halibut.

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:06.880
See, you should just wait when you're in trouble, baby

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:10.550
All right. You're a rare alien, aren't you?

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:13.930
Will you come with me to get registered at the Alien Registration Center?

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:18.390
So where did Dandy end by being sent?

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:23.980
According to the GPS on his phone, he's on Planet Pushy Boyfriend.

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:26.230
That's pretty far...

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:29.150
We'd by there in a second if we used that light,

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:32.070
but then the person holding the light wouldn't be able to go,

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:35.110
and we'd need the light to get back.

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:39.700
And it looks like it'd need a lot of power to shine on the whole ship.

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:43.120
Speaking of which, the light already seems a little dimmer.

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:46.630
About how much power is left?

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:47.710
What're these?

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:51.710
Oh, they don't sell batteries like these anymore, huh?

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:55.220
Aw jeez, I'm too hungry to think!

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:03.430
Maybe...

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:05.640
What is it?

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:09.270
What?

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:14.110
Oh, Meow! You're here!

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:16.450
It's all right. Come over here!

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:22.540
There's a hole around here 
so be careful!!
 Don't move!!

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:25.290
What are you waiting for? You're so slow!

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:26.250
Watch out!! Go around!!

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:37.220
Man, I should've stayed slow and steady.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:48.650
It's faster if you climb this way.

00:09:57.740 --> 00:09:59.490
The halibut from earlier is above us now!

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:02.240
Oh, what's that?

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:13.800
Dr. Gel, I have determined Dandy's location.

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:15.960
Don't you say that every time?

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:18.090
I am confident this time.

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:21.970
All right, watch out, Dandy!

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:31.360
So, to put it simply,

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:36.360
you came from that planet to investigate this place with the encouragement of your people,

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:38.570
but your rocket crashed so you couldn't go back,

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:43.330
and now ten years have passed without you being able to contact anyone. Right?

00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:58.130
That's right.

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:03.890
Listen, that guy's a genuine unregistered alien.

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:07.520
Even the translator had trouble with his language at first.

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:09.060
I can't take it anymore.

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:12.560
I'm so hungry, all I see is dinner when I look at him.

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:17.150
He promised to go to the Alien Registration Center is we cooperate with him.

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:19.190
Bear with it a little longer!

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:24.280
I studied this planet for ten years.

00:11:25.490 --> 00:11:29.580
The caves branching out in the middle of the planet

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:34.040
were created by the roots of a giants tree and left behind when the tree burned up.

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:38.920
It appears to have been burned up in thousand-year cycles after that,

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:44.550
so it can be inferred that it comes into contact with a sun-like star with the same cycle.

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:51.390
My planet, Planet Girlfriend, has been a satellite of this planet for about a hundred years,

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:55.650
and it's been just over a thousand years since the last time this planet burned up,

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:59.190
so the sun could come again at any minute.

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:04.450
If the sun comes, my planet will probably not be able to escape being burned up with it.

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:10.580
If science continued its progress, my people should have noticed,

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:13.540
but I must return to Girlfriend quickly!

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:16.380
Why don't you just zip over using that light?

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:20.550
N-No, he can't! The battery's almost dead.

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:23.760
I've got <i>this</i>!

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:27.800
A boat made from the wreckage of my rocket.

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:32.560
I want to use this to climb the water pillar to get to my planet.

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:34.480
Why haven't you done it already?

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:38.150
Because it was too heavy to life to the surface...

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:47.950
Aw, stop being so stingy. Just use the light!

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:50.160
It's not like it's that far.

00:12:58.880 --> 00:12:59.920
Huh?

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:03.170
The battery's dead?!

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:09.850
Isn't this light enough to be carried now?

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:12.850
Forget that, the battery's dead!

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:14.940
Aw man, we can't go back now.

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:15.730
Why?

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:21.150
These are the same as the batteries on my planet.

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:23.990
They're a dime a dozen back there.

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:25.150
Huh?

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:38.580
It's so light!

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:42.800
B-But it still weighs about 100 kilograms.

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:45.670
Keep trying, young man!

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:50.510
If we can get that guy to the registration center, 
we'll get a ton of money!

00:13:51.140 --> 00:13:56.140
He just looks like walking food to me now...

00:13:56.520 --> 00:14:00.270
If this plan succeeds, you'll able to eat anything you want.

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:18.000
It's here!

00:14:47.940 --> 00:14:50.030
Well, how are we going to get to your planet?

00:14:50.910 --> 00:14:51.490
Like this—

00:14:54.530 --> 00:14:55.870
And then?

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:57.040
See ya!

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:58.040
Hey!

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:03.710
There's less gravity up there.

00:15:41.160 --> 00:15:42.750
As expected of a cat.

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:45.090
I'm a Betelgeusian!

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:46.250
If it's come to this—

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:49.510
You're nimble. This should be a piece of cake for you!

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:51.420
No, it's impossible!

00:15:51.420 --> 00:15:54.010
Do you want to be stuck on this planet forever?

00:15:54.010 --> 00:15:56.760
That doesn't sound like a bad idea!

00:15:56.760 --> 00:16:00.140
There aren't any cute girls here!

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:10.110
It's salt.

00:16:10.110 --> 00:16:11.530
It's so salty!

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:25.000
It looks like a lot of time has passed.

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:27.840
Shouldn't we go look for that guy?

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:30.760
Naw, let's relax and wait here.

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:33.590
He might come back, you know.

00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:36.800
There are a lot of holes here, too!

00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:44.520
There's a strange town down there.

00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:50.690
Yoko!

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:54.990
Yoko, I came back!

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:57.030
I'm back from Pushy Boyfriend!

00:16:57.030 --> 00:17:01.290
There was an alien! We're not the only ones in space!

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:03.460
Really?

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:05.460
It's a huge anthropological discovery!

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:07.580
The future will be changed forever!

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:13.590
After you left. Planet Girlfriend changed its course.

00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:17.260
Knowing about space isn't worth a thing.

00:17:17.260 --> 00:17:21.510
I finally made it back, so your parents will accept us now...

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:23.430
Minato!

00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:25.600
Good job making it back alive.

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:30.070
But it seems you do not understand the situation you are in.

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:37.860
It's been a hundred years since you left for Pushy Boyfriend.

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:40.030
You haven't changed much,

00:17:40.030 --> 00:17:44.750
but we've gone through a lot of trouble to stay looking like this.

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:49.540
We've raised many grandchildren,

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:53.800
and great-grandchildren, all the way to great-great-great grandchildren.

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:05.350
This planet will be caught by the sun!

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:08.100
I figured it out after doing research on Pushy Boyfriend!

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:11.270
We must leave immediately! We have to hurry!

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:24.910
There you go exaggerating again.

00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:27.500
Are you that jealous of the success of others?

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:31.250
You were an eyesore to the rest of us on this planet.

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:34.460
That other planet suited you a lot better.

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:35.960
The hell with that!

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:39.050
I worked hard for ten years to save the world!

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:40.930
This guy's hopeless.

00:18:39.050 --> 00:18:40.930
I was... I was...

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:50.150
Everyone! The sun is coming!

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:52.980
You have to run away! The sun is coming!

00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:55.280
That person's naked.

00:18:56.190 --> 00:18:58.190
Oh, batteries.

00:18:58.650 --> 00:19:00.200
Got 'em!

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:03.200
I got some batteries!

00:19:03.950 --> 00:19:05.030
Look!

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:08.620
Hm? Does it seem like it got hotter to you?

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:11.880
Well...

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:14.840
Woah, did that just get a whole lot bigger?

00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:24.220
They stink. They all stink!

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:27.180
Well? Do you feel like coming with us now?

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:31.350
Everyone on this planet should just be broiled in a salt crust!

00:19:31.350 --> 00:19:32.560
Alien Registration Cent—

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:33.900
Hot, hot, hot!

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:35.400
I'm going to go bald!

00:19:37.690 --> 00:19:39.900
Everyone should just burn...

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:44.320
Everyone, everyone, everyone should just burn...!

00:19:44.320 --> 00:19:45.660
Wait... Hot, hot!

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:48.660
Burn my body to a crisp!

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:52.870
You can't get scorched!

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:55.670
Look c'mon... it's too hot!

00:19:56.420 --> 00:19:59.670
Yoko... Yoko...!

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:08.010
I guess that's what happens when a man's jealousy flares up.

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:16.650
Is he even worth bringing back?

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:20.400
Well then...

00:20:22.530 --> 00:20:23.950
Damn it!

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:40.380
I have finally found you, Dandy.

00:20:40.380 --> 00:20:42.840
You should resign yourself to your fate.

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:49.930
Oh, are you planning on running away? 
You won't make it at the rate you're going.

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:54.350
Liberty Beam, prepare to fire!

00:20:59.730 --> 00:21:01.150
What's wrong, Bea?

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:03.570
It seems really hot in here...

00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:05.240
I'm burning!

00:21:36.020 --> 00:21:39.810
It was probably an unregistered alien after all, wasn't it?

00:21:39.810 --> 00:21:43.690
We can't register it now that it's become a grilled fish, though.

00:21:45.490 --> 00:21:48.700
Well, I guess we'll just have to eat it.

00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:50.950
Hurray!

00:21:59.040 --> 00:22:00.460
It's so good...

00:22:01.170 --> 00:22:03.550
It's just like I said—

00:22:03.550 --> 00:22:07.300
You'll come by delicious food if you use that light.

00:22:07.300 --> 00:22:09.890
That was a very round about way to do it, wasn't it?

00:22:09.890 --> 00:22:11.970
And we almost died a bunch of times.

00:22:12.390 --> 00:22:14.140
That's how the way it is, isn't it?

00:22:14.140 --> 00:22:15.890
No matter the time or place—

00:22:15.890 --> 00:22:19.270
Slow and steady winds the race, baby.

